{
  "dom_id": "step-q171725",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A horizontal line $l$ passes through the point $(-3,2).$ What are the coordinates of the $y$-intercept of $l?$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept of $l$ are\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$",
  "worked_solution": "On any horizontal line, all points have the same $y$-coordinate.\n\nThe $y$-coordinate of the point $(-3,2)$ is $2,$ so the $y$-coordinate of the $y$-intercept is also $2.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,2).$",
